/* The truncation of `x - sin x`'s series in spacelab-propagation `shadow::x_minus_sin`, certified
   (plans/17 Ф28.B).

   Below x = 2 the code sums x^3/3! - x^5/5! + x^7/7! Q with Q's Horner chain over n = 8, 10, ..., 24,
   which in exact arithmetic is the Taylor polynomial to x^25/25!: every coefficient is exact (the
   leading terms are double-double, the divisions are by exact small integers at run time), so the
   approximation is that polynomial and its rounding is x_minus_sin_roundoff.mac's. The doc comment
   says the first term left out, x^27/27!, bounds the truncation under 1.2e-20 of the sum.

   `split` encloses sup |p/f - 1| over [0, 2], f = x - sin x, whose zero of order 3 at 0 the
   polynomial shares.

   cd derivations && timeout 300 sollya shadow_x_minus_sin_supnorm.sollya                        */

execute("supnorm_lib.sollya");

p = 0;
for k from 1 to 12 do p = p + (-1)^(k + 1) * x^(2*k + 1) / fact(2*k + 1);

split("shadow_x_minus_sin", p, x - sin(x), 2, 40);
quit;
